IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Row il-48. NOUNS of a cross-reference and of a printed figure. No rule is written here; the facts below are what a reader of the texts could state.
-- TARGET COMPILER: main. No REFUSE, no section GIVEN, no TYPICALLY, no YMD, no sets: a case the sources do not answer is NOTHING from a MAYBE.
--
-- This row is NOT an encoding of the Minimum Wage Law, 5747-1987. It records citations: for each, what the citing words say they point at, what the target is,
-- and where each of the two readings comes from. A citation whose two descriptions differ is a defect, and is kept in an expected-red file.
--
-- THE KINDS BELOW ARE MINE, not the Law's: each is a short plain description I wrote from reading the citing words and the target, so that two descriptions of the same
-- thing are the same kind. The words of the texts are quoted beside each value in the references module (`src:` lines are the Minimum Wage Law consolidation,
-- `ext:[youth]`, `ext:[nii]` and `ext:[interp]` lines are the other consolidations, `ext:[SH ...]` and `ext:[KT ...]` lines are typed from a page image of the official instrument).

§ `Nouns of a cross-reference`

DECLARE `What a provision is about` IS ONE OF
    `section 3(ג) of the Law as made: the rule on counting a premium as a pay component`
    `a subsection of the Law that was repealed, so that the section prints no text for it`
    `the fixed addition paid to the worker because of the work, which section 3(ב)(3) of the Law lists as a pay component`
    `the definition of the average wage in section 1 of the National Insurance Law [Consolidated Version], 5728-1968`
    `the definition of the average wage in section 1 of the National Insurance Law [Consolidated Version], 5755-1995`
    `the three conditions of section 6א(א) under which the right to the minimum wage lies also against the actual employer`

-- Three kinds of reading, from the strongest to the weakest.
-- The second kind is the honest name for most limbs here: the official page was read, but that no LATER instrument touched the words rests on the consolidation's list of amending instruments.
DECLARE `Where a reading comes from` IS ONE OF
    `the official instrument, read from its page image`
    `the official instruments read from their page images; that no later instrument touched the words is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
    `the consolidation only`

DECLARE `A cross-reference` HAS
    `the citing words are in` IS A STRING
    `the citing words say it points at` IS A `What a provision is about`
    `the target is` IS A `What a provision is about`
    `the text the citing words name stopped being the text in force on` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `read through the Interpretation Law section 25 the citing words reach` IS A MAYBE `What a provision is about`
    `limb (a) was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`
    `limb (b) was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`

§ `Nouns of a printed figure`

DECLARE `A printed figure` HAS
    `what the figure is` IS A STRING
    `the official instrument prints` IS A NUMBER
    `the deposited consolidation prints` IS A NUMBER
    `the official figure was read from` IS A `Where a reading comes from`
